# Why bubble sort is so slow
subtitle: "Watch bubble sort swap neighbours one pair at a time, count the swaps it must make, then sort six bars yourself and beat it."

## Why bubble sort is so slow
use: bubble_sort
with: {"values":[5,2,8,1,9,3]}

    hide hint counter

    card title "Why bubble sort is so slow"

Why is bubble sort so slow? Six bars show it. Its one rule: only neighbours may swap.
    draw bar_0 bar_1 bar_2 bar_3 bar_4 bar_5 parallel true

Five stands before two, so they swap.
    move bar_0 path [[68.335,90],[136.67,0]]

    move bar_1 by [-136.67,0]

Then it walks along the row. Five and eight are in order, but eight and one are not, so they swap too.
    move bar_2 path [[68.335,90],[136.67,0]]

    move bar_3 by [-136.67,0]

Eight and nine are fine; nine and three swap. One pass has carried the tallest bar to the end.
    move bar_4 path [[68.335,90],[136.67,0]]

    move bar_5 by [-136.67,0]

But each pass settles just one bar for sure, so it takes pass after pass.
    highlight bar_4

So how many swaps in all? Go back to the starting row, and count the pairs that stand in the wrong order.
    move bar_0 bar_2 bar_4 by [-136.67,0]

    move bar_1 bar_3 bar_5 by [136.67,0]

Five stands ahead of three smaller bars, two ahead of one, eight ahead of two, nine ahead of one: seven in all.
    text t0 "3" #b5482e x 158.3 y 433.3 font_size 40
    text t1 "1" #b5482e x 295 y 323.3 font_size 40
    text t2 "2" #b5482e x 431.7 y 543.3 font_size 40
    text t3 "0" #b5482e x 568.3 y 286.7 font_size 40
    text t4 "1" #b5482e x 705 y 580 font_size 40
    text t5 "0" #b5482e x 841.7 y 360 font_size 40
    text sum "7 wrong pairs" #b5482e x 260 y 655 font_size 42

A neighbour swap fixes exactly one wrong pair and disturbs no other. So bubble sort makes exactly seven swaps; our first pass made three of them.
    highlight sum

    erase t0 t1 t2 t3 t4 t5 sum

Worst case, a row in reverse: every pair is wrong. With n bars, that is n times n minus one, over two.
    math pairs tex "\\text{pairs} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}" size 34 x 500 y 600

    erase pairs

A thousand bars: half a million swaps. A million bars: five hundred billion.
    text big "1,000,000 bars: 500 billion swaps" x 500 y 655 font_size 42

    erase big

Faster sorts, like merge sort, compare items far apart. A million items take them about twenty million steps instead.
    text ms "merge sort: 20 million" #2f6b8f x 500 y 655 font_size 42

No wonder Donald Knuth judged that bubble sort has nothing to recommend it, except a catchy name.
    portrait portrait_donald_knuth x 130 y 600 width 110 of "Donald Knuth" cameo true

    erase portrait_donald_knuth ms

Now sort these six yourself, one neighbour swap at a time.
    draw counter

    ask "Sort the bars. Can you do it in seven swaps?" widget bubble_sort answer sorted
        right: Seven swaps, one for each pair that stood in the wrong order.
        wrong: Only neighbours may swap: drag a bar onto the one beside it.

    quiz "Ten bars in reverse order. How many swaps?"
        right: 45: all ten times nine over two pairs are in the wrong order, and each swap fixes just one.
        * 10
        + 45
        * 100
---
